<title>UK: Daimler - over half units meet capital return goal.</title>
<headline>Daimler - over half units meet capital return goal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>German industrial conglomerate Daimler-Benz AG said on Thursday that more than half of its 23 businesses had already reached or improved on its target 12 percent return on capital employed.</p>
<p>&quot;More than half have now matched or exceeded the target,&quot; chief executive Juergen Schrempp told the interim results conference held in London.</p>
<p>Schrempp said earlier that the group as a whole was on course to meet the 12 percent target in two years.</p>
<p>--Tony Roddam, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
